Subject: [PATCH] Use literal format strings in printf-like calls
Origin: https://src.opensuse.org/pool/cvs/src/branch/factory/compile-with-Wformat-security.patch

Treat the existing strings as data so hardened format-security flags do
not reject these calls.
---
diff --git a/diff/diff3.c b/diff/diff3.c
--- a/diff/diff3.c
+++ b/diff/diff3.c
@@ -1506 +1506 @@ output_diff3 (diff, mapping, rev_mapping)
-		  printf_output (line_prefix);
+		  printf_output ("%s", line_prefix);
diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -1461 +1461 @@ usage (register const char *const *cpp)
-	(void) fprintf (stderr, *cpp);
+	(void) fprintf (stderr, "%s", *cpp);
